From 4d3d4b61022b5786cafde3b12c11d2dbb2b51a7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:35:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cli): exit 2 instead of panicking on stderr, args or
 --timeout

The CLI promises exit codes 0, 1 and 2, but several inputs ended in a
panic, exit 101 (#594):

- every diagnostic and the inspect trailer used eprintln!, which panics
  when stderr is closed or full. Writes now go through a checked helper;
  a lost diagnostic keeps its exit 2, and a trailer that cannot be written
  is exit 2.
- std::env::args panics on an argument that is not UTF-8. Arguments are
  read with args_os: termlens's own options and operands must be UTF-8 and
  are refused with exit 2, while the program inspect runs and its
  arguments pass through untouched.
- Instant::now() + --timeout overflowed for a huge value after the program
  was spawned. A timeout the clock cannot add is refused by name.
- render --out "" printed the filesystem's complaint; it now says --out
  needs a PATH argument, as --out= already did (#451).

The inspect example gets the same fixes, including its println! of --help
under | true.

Signed-off-by: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
